groom's and develop's `run` machines share `index.md` and the edge `awaiting-approval →
ready-for-dev`, each with its own hooks, so a move naming no `--playbook` is refused listing both
candidates, and the plan keeps its status.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan/index.md --
---
title: Plan
status: awaiting-approval
---
# Plan
-- cmd --
booping transition plan/index.md ready-for-dev
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: {CWD}/plan/index.md matches more than one machine with an edge awaiting-approval → ready-for-dev: develop/run, groom/run; pass --playbook
